Rebased on latest main (clean replay, no conflicts). Still needs the `ready` label to unblock full CI.

@mgoin — re-review when you get a chance? All earlier feedback was addressed (guard centralised in `marlin_utils` covering all Marlin paths + auto-compat-lib detection in `env_override.py`).

@robertgshaw2-redhat @yewentao256 @pavanimajety @tlrmchlsmth — also pinging the requested reviewers. Thanks!

@mgoin rebased onto current main — the merge conflict is resolved and the PR is mergeable again. Pre-commit and the guard tests pass locally (`tests/quantization/test_marlin_toolchain_guard.py`, 8 passed).

The fix is no longer AWQ-local: the guard is centralised in `marlin_utils` and now fires from every Marlin path (`check_marlin_supported`, `verify_marlin_supported`, dense + MoE layer checks), with auto compat-lib detection in `env_override.py` so users can still load the kernel. That covers your earlier "too local / let users keep the kernel" feedback.

Could you take another look, and add the `ready` label to unblock CI? Thanks!

